## Start gate

Required completed exports: [Electronic definitions and schematics](Schematics.lingua); [Exact assembly geometry and interference](Exact-Assemblies.lingua); [Revisioned model quantities and takeoff](Takeoff.lingua)

Dependency reason: Board realization needs electronic topology plus geometry/clearance and quantity outputs. It can proceed beside functional-device implementation.

This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

Two-layer placement/routing/vias, electrical/board checks, enclosure comparison and versioned BOM/artwork/drill/placement exports.

## Ownership and possible overlap

PCB geometry/check/export adapters and layout UI; no separate save or net identity system.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 11a.T04

- [ ] **11a.T04.** Deliver footprint assignment, board outline/stackup, placement/rotation, keepouts, trace routing and through-via editing. Derive copper connectivity and geometric checks through bounded jobs keyed to the accepted revision. Show unrouted connections and conflicts; integrate board/enclosure clearance through existing CAD/assembly selections. Do not require the electrical graph to be a tree.

### Task 11a.T05

- [ ] **11a.T05.** Implement the supported electrical-rule checks for pin roles, missing required supply/reference connections, unconnected required pins and conflicting declared drivers. Implement board checks for net shorts, opens, minimum clearance, width, drill/pad bounds and board-edge clearance within B43's geometry subset. Preserve waived diagnostics with reason and source revision; stale or incomplete analysis is not a pass. These are declared design-rule checks, not general electrical correctness certification.

### Task 11a.T06

- [ ] **11a.T06.** Export a revision-pinned bill of materials, machine-readable connectivity, placement data, supported copper/mask/outline artwork and drill data. Choose and document the exact Gerber/drill/placement subsets against independent readers and a reviewed fixture; preserve units, origin, rotations and top/bottom conventions. Unsupported manufacturing outputs remain unavailable rather than plausible approximations. Imports preserve lineage, mapping conflicts and permitted library dependencies without fetching or executing arbitrary referenced content.

